---
import TopicPage from '../../components/TopicPage.astro';
import AccordionItem from '../../components/AccordionItem.astro';
---

<TopicPage title="Emergency buffer" slug="emergency-buffer">
	<div class="space-y-5">
		<p>
			One of the first and most important things regardless of your goals is to ensure you have some money to fall back
			on in the event of an emergency. Usually, it is recommended to have <span class="whitespace-nowrap">3-6</span> times your usual essential monthly
			expenses.
		</p>
		<p>
			However, it’s usually not smart or feasible to raise this amount of capital straight away, especially when you
			have to neglect other things to do it – high-interest debt, pension matching, etc. So, it can be a more sensible
			approach to save just one month’s worth of essential expenses.
		</p>
	</div>

	<div class="mt-8 space-y-3">
		<AccordionItem question="What is an emergency buffer for?">
			<p>
				This emergency buffer will allow you to handle unexpected costs such as vet bills, car repairs, emergency
				dentist treatment, etc. All without having to take out loans, use credit cards, etc.
			</p>
		</AccordionItem>

		<AccordionItem question="How do I make an emergency buffer?">
			<p>
				Making an emergency buffer is straightforward. Open up an easy-access savings account, then deposit a
				predetermined amount every time you receive your pay.
			</p>
		</AccordionItem>

		<AccordionItem question="What happens if I use my emergency buffer?">
			<p>
				If you need to use your emergency buffer, that’s okay! That’s exactly what it’s there for, to help you when
				something unplanned happens. The important thing is to make sure that your first priority is ensuring that it
				gets filled back up again before continuing with any of the following sections.
			</p>
		</AccordionItem>
	</div>
</TopicPage>
